		<author>
			<name>Giampiero Fiorelli</name>
		</author>
		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;A few days ago we reported about the exclusive &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt; installation at &lt;strong&gt;Harvey Nichols London&lt;/strong&gt;, showcasing specially commisioned pieces by &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt; from the film &lt;strong&gt;W.E.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We can finally show you a few photographs of the installations thanks to &lt;strong&gt;Harvey Nichols London&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet Paris&lt;/strong&gt;. Enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/01.jpg&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; alt=&quot;W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London&quot; width=&quot;790&quot; height=&quot;1053&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/02.jpg&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; alt=&quot;W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London&quot; width=&quot;790&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/03.jpg&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; alt=&quot;W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London&quot; width=&quot;790&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://drownedmadonna.com/img/2011/harvey-nichols/04.jpg&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; alt=&quot;W.E. Vionnet Harvey Nicholson London&quot; width=&quot;790&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harvey Nichols London&lt;/strong&gt; is hosting the special Vionnet installation till September 30 in a dedicated space on the First Floor of the store. The installation is providing customers with the unique opportunity to view the special archive pieces from the film.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Harvey Nichols&lt;/strong&gt; is the perfect place to showcase the intricate and exquisite pieces and will allow customers to truly appreciate the attention to detail and craftsmanship of the House&quot;   explains &lt;strong&gt;Matteo Marzotto&lt;/strong&gt;, CEO of &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt;.   &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt; worked alongside director Madonna and costume designer &lt;strong&gt;Arianne Phillips&lt;/strong&gt; to re-create original &lt;strong&gt;Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt; pieces from &lt;strong&gt;Wallis Simpsons&lt;/strong&gt; wardrobe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The installation is providing customers with a greater awareness of the unique heritage and vision of &lt;strong&gt;Madeleine Vionnet&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vionnet Installation,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;14th- 30th September 2011&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Harvey Nichols,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knightsbridge London,&lt;/p&gt;
