	<entry>
		<title>Gossip: Reportedly Lourdes judged the London's dance auditions and will be one of the dancers on Madonna's Next Tour</title>
		<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/122-reportedly-lourdes-judged-the-londons-dance-auditions-for-madonnas-next-tour.html"/>
		<published>2011-09-26T00:03:38Z</published>
		<updated>2011-09-26T00:03:38Z</updated>
		<id>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/122-reportedly-lourdes-judged-the-londons-dance-auditions-for-madonnas-next-tour.html</id>
		<author>
			<name>Giampiero Fiorelli</name>
		</author>
		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We at DrownedMadonna.com were the first to break the news of &lt;strong&gt;dance auditions&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;London's Pineapple Dance Studios&lt;/strong&gt; for &lt;strong&gt;Madonna's next tour&lt;/strong&gt;, as part of &lt;strong&gt;Smirnoff Nightlife Exchange Project&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Besides uploading their one-minute video online, applicants had the chance to audition in New York and &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;. New York's dance audition took place with choreographers Tony and Rich Talauega as judges on September 8, while London casting call took place last Friday and no judges were announced.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But according to a gossip published on today's &lt;strong&gt;Daily Star&lt;/strong&gt;, hordes of dancers in &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt; were surprised to find out that &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt;'s daugher, &lt;strong&gt;Lourdes&lt;/strong&gt;, was there to judge them. According to the British tabloid, Lola has been a pupil at the &lt;strong&gt;Pineapple Studios&lt;/strong&gt; for years and she has perfected a mix of styles now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reportedly, &lt;strong&gt;Lourdes&lt;/strong&gt; will join the team of &lt;strong&gt;dancers&lt;/strong&gt; on &lt;strong&gt;Madonna's next tour&lt;/strong&gt; and promo-tour. &quot;&lt;strong&gt;Lourdes&lt;/strong&gt; does routines every day in her mum’s studios as well as taking classes,&quot; a source told &lt;strong&gt;the Star&lt;/strong&gt;. &quot;She can now do jazz, hip-hop, popping, contemporary and even tap. That's why she is qualified to judge who would be the best back-up dancers for her mum.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; is confirmed by Live Nation for the final dance competition on November 12 in New York City, when one dancer will be chosen for her next tour, in collaboration with &lt;strong&gt;Smirnoff&lt;/strong&gt; as part of a multi-deal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedTags&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Smirnoff&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Dancers Auditions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;London&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lourdes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
